1
00:01:06,316 --> 00:01:08,735
I forgot to bring your shirt.

2
00:01:10,130 --> 00:01:11,505
I don't care.

3
00:01:18,370 --> 00:01:19,987
I don't care anymore.

4
00:01:25,794 --> 00:01:29,929
I... But I've never done this before.

5
00:01:31,005 --> 00:01:32,716
Do you want to stop?

6
00:02:02,331 --> 00:02:04,989
I don't even know your name.

7
00:02:13,925 --> 00:02:15,511
Cho Yu Gyeom.

8
00:02:16,751 --> 00:02:20,709
[2. I Never Wanted to Die]

9
00:02:21,683 --> 00:02:26,509
[Episode 2]
Honey, what's Pro Cho Ji Hyeon like?

10
00:02:26,509 --> 00:02:29,107
- So-so.
- I see.

11
00:02:29,107 --> 00:02:35,302
I heard that family's a big deal around here.

12
00:02:36,083 --> 00:02:39,008
They say they're practically royalty.

13
00:02:39,726 --> 00:02:43,497
Well, he was pretty down-to-earth, though.

14
00:02:43,497 --> 00:02:45,209
Yeah.

15
00:02:45,209 --> 00:02:49,878
Oh, right. Jung Yeon,
when do you have to go back to Seoul?

16
00:02:49,878 --> 00:02:51,321
The day after tomorrow.

17
00:02:51,321 --> 00:02:55,133
Then when you go,
could you bring me what's in the fridge?

18
00:02:55,133 --> 00:02:58,178
I left some things there.
I'm worried they'll spoil.

19
00:02:59,096 --> 00:03:01,014
- Jung Yeon?
- Yes?

20
00:03:01,014 --> 00:03:03,310
- Where are you going?
- To the fridge.

21
00:03:03,310 --> 00:03:06,160
Oh my. What's wrong with him?

22
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:09,259
I mean the fridge at our house
in Seoul, not this one.

23
00:03:10,176 --> 00:03:12,710
What's gotten into you?

24
00:03:12,710 --> 00:03:14,883
Didn't you sleep last night either?

25
00:03:15,821 --> 00:03:18,593
- I'm fine.
- Honestly.

26
00:03:18,593 --> 00:03:20,500
You need sleep, or your body will...

27
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:24,287
- Oh, Kim Ha Yeon.
- Yeah?

28
00:03:24,287 --> 00:03:28,400
I signed you up for supplementary classes
at the local school,

29
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:31,837
so you can start going today.

30
00:03:31,837 --> 00:03:36,493
- What?
- You kept going on about it.

31
00:03:36,493 --> 00:03:39,550
So you're telling me to go to school here now?

32
00:03:39,550 --> 00:03:43,390
Just the supplementary classes. That's all.

33
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:46,542
- And that's at...?
- One o'clock.

34
00:03:46,542 --> 00:03:50,417
Right. Just go to Upo High School
by one o'clock.

35
00:03:50,417 --> 00:03:52,444
I already called them.

36
00:03:52,444 --> 00:03:56,618
Then go to the teachers' office. Take this.

37
00:03:58,947 --> 00:04:01,408
They have programs like that these days?

38
00:04:01,408 --> 00:04:05,187
Yes, apparently.
Even kids from abroad can sign up.

39
00:04:05,187 --> 00:04:09,876
Seriously! Without even telling me!

40
00:04:09,876 --> 00:04:12,718
Seriously.

41
00:04:49,789 --> 00:04:51,416
Yu Gyeom!

42
00:04:52,459 --> 00:04:54,169
Cho Yu Gyeom!

43
00:04:56,667 --> 00:04:59,963
Come eat! Hurry, hurry!

44
00:05:35,585 --> 00:05:37,818
Cho Yu Gyeom.

45
00:05:37,818 --> 00:05:41,442
Did you run your father's errand yesterday?

46
00:05:43,310 --> 00:05:48,430
He did great, Father. Really great.
Right, Yu Gyeom?

47
00:05:48,430 --> 00:05:51,182
Yes, Grandfather. It went just fine.

48
00:05:51,182 --> 00:05:53,707
What errand did you run?

49
00:05:55,855 --> 00:05:58,130
- Soy sauce...
- Changnyeong!

50
00:06:09,119 --> 00:06:10,829
Yu Gyeom's mother.

51
00:06:10,829 --> 00:06:12,396
I want a word with you.

52
00:06:16,047 --> 00:06:21,709
If you can't even look after one child,
how do you expect to be part of this family?

53
00:06:21,709 --> 00:06:23,078
Even now...

54
00:06:31,891 --> 00:06:35,854
I'm the one who lied,
and you're the one who skipped out on it,

55
00:06:36,688 --> 00:06:40,115
but your grandfather's such a pain. Right?

56
00:06:41,651 --> 00:06:44,739
If he's that annoying,
you should say something, Dad.

57
00:06:44,739 --> 00:06:48,825
Say, "Father, you're being quite a pain."

58
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:51,478
No way. I'm scared.

59
00:07:05,425 --> 00:07:09,096
- Don't run. Hello.
- Hello.

60
00:07:12,626 --> 00:07:15,953
- Hello
- Hello.

61
00:07:20,396 --> 00:07:22,728
- Hello
- Hello.

62
00:07:29,783 --> 00:07:35,956
Okay, listen up. Starting today, she'll join
our supplementary classes for the vacation.

63
00:07:35,956 --> 00:07:37,938
Kim Ha Yeon.

64
00:07:44,047 --> 00:07:46,807
You could at least clap.

65
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:53,432
You can sit in that empty seat over there.

66
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:05,552
I'm taking attendance.

67
00:08:05,552 --> 00:08:08,472
- Goh Hui Jun.
- Here.

68
00:08:08,472 --> 00:08:10,530
- Kim Gi Nam.
- Here.

69
00:08:11,741 --> 00:08:14,244
- Kim Jin Mi.
- Here.

70
00:08:14,244 --> 00:08:16,167
- Kim Hye Won.
- Here.

71
00:08:16,167 --> 00:08:18,040
- Ryu Si Yeon.
- Here.

72
00:08:19,082 --> 00:08:21,543
- Sung Sae Ryeong.
- Here.

73
00:08:21,543 --> 00:08:23,795
Turn it all in by next class.

74
00:08:44,483 --> 00:08:46,590
Hey, what are you looking at?

75
00:08:54,659 --> 00:08:57,194
- Young master.
- Cho Yu Gyeom.

76
00:08:57,194 --> 00:09:01,703
- Are you better at freestyle or butterfly?
- I'm good at all of them.

77
00:09:20,977 --> 00:09:22,103
Hey, who's that?

78
00:09:22,103 --> 00:09:24,670
Wow, total attention seeker.

79
00:09:50,006 --> 00:09:51,572
I'm Cho Yu Gyeom.

80
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:53,967
And you?

81
00:09:56,513 --> 00:09:58,891
I'm Kim Ha Yeon.

82
00:10:01,392 --> 00:10:03,006
What?

83
00:10:03,006 --> 00:10:05,839
Nothing. You have a pretty name.

84
00:10:16,825 --> 00:10:18,348
Cho Yu Gyeom!

85
00:10:19,083 --> 00:10:20,754
Wait for me!

86
00:10:25,293 --> 00:10:26,609
Do you know her?

87
00:10:56,292 --> 00:11:00,292
Kim Ha Yeon. I have to go out again for a bit.

88
00:11:00,292 --> 00:11:03,997
Get Jung Yeon some dinner. Kim Ha Yeon?

89
00:11:08,293 --> 00:11:10,066
Seriously. That girl.

90
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:57,295
Thanks for giving it back.

91
00:11:59,719 --> 00:12:02,681
I didn't return it. I threw it away.

92
00:12:08,174 --> 00:12:11,982
I told you, I threw that away.

93
00:12:21,754 --> 00:12:23,826
What are you doing tonight?

94
00:12:23,826 --> 00:12:26,346
But you have a girlfriend, don't you?

95
00:12:26,346 --> 00:12:28,418
I asked what you're doing tonight!

96
00:12:29,944 --> 00:12:32,267
Go hang out with your girlfriend!

97
00:12:33,252 --> 00:12:35,537
My girlfriend's going to hang out with you?

98
00:12:35,537 --> 00:12:40,008
No! I mean you should hang out with her!

99
00:13:33,855 --> 00:13:37,164
But why did you do that with me
when you have a girlfriend?

100
00:13:37,817 --> 00:13:39,761
You approached me first.

101
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:45,798
So even with a girlfriend,
you let anyone who makes a move get close?

102
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:51,807
Who knows?

103
00:13:52,466 --> 00:13:54,250
"Who knows"?

104
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:56,044
Yeah. Who knows.

105
00:13:58,337 --> 00:14:00,590
Seriously. You crazy bastard!

106
00:14:00,590 --> 00:14:02,859
- Hey!
- What?

107
00:14:09,265 --> 00:14:11,281
Take this. It's yours.

108
00:14:18,858 --> 00:14:21,110
How did you find this?

109
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:22,944
In the sea.

110
00:14:22,944 --> 00:14:24,197
What?

111
00:14:24,197 --> 00:14:27,250
I dried it off.
You can try turning it on tomorrow morning.

112
00:14:27,250 --> 00:14:30,502
But since it fell in the sea,
it might be a little corroded.

113
00:14:37,043 --> 00:14:39,738
Okay. Thanks.

114
00:14:42,131 --> 00:14:43,800
What are you doing tonight?

115
00:14:45,984 --> 00:14:47,901
I want to see you, okay?

116
00:14:49,806 --> 00:14:52,169
Want to meet here at 9:30 p.m.?

117
00:14:52,169 --> 00:14:53,810
No!

118
00:14:53,810 --> 00:14:55,443
I'll wait!

119
00:14:55,443 --> 00:14:57,548
I said no!

120
00:14:57,548 --> 00:14:59,295
Until you come!

121
00:14:59,295 --> 00:15:01,317
I said no!

122
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:14,288
How did you find this?

123
00:15:14,288 --> 00:15:15,729
In the sea.

124
00:16:11,971 --> 00:16:15,101
What do you think? Want to go in together?

125
00:16:35,968 --> 00:16:37,663
No.

126
00:16:37,663 --> 00:16:38,715
Okay.

127
00:16:40,415 --> 00:16:42,083
I'll get going then.

128
00:16:55,181 --> 00:16:58,602
I dreamed I was with you.

129
00:16:59,477 --> 00:17:02,940
But in the dream, I knew it was a dream.

130
00:17:35,471 --> 00:17:37,464
I want to see you, okay?

131
00:17:37,464 --> 00:17:39,581
Want to meet here at 9:30 p.m.?

132
00:17:42,646 --> 00:17:46,033
Hey, Mom wants you to come out.

133
00:17:48,359 --> 00:17:49,792
What are you doing?

134
00:18:09,922 --> 00:18:13,594
Did you see the text Mom sent you yesterday?

135
00:18:14,343 --> 00:18:15,579
No.

136
00:18:15,579 --> 00:18:16,935
Why not?

137
00:18:18,222 --> 00:18:20,559
My phone fell in the sea.

138
00:18:21,517 --> 00:18:22,991
What?

139
00:18:22,991 --> 00:18:25,071
It'll turn on tomorrow, I guess.

140
00:18:27,523 --> 00:18:30,819
Kim Ha Yeon. What's gotten into you lately?

141
00:18:30,819 --> 00:18:32,075
What did I do?

142
00:18:32,075 --> 00:18:37,552
Why do you keep talking back?
And you never listen.

143
00:18:37,552 --> 00:18:41,034
You yell at everything I say,
and you go out without telling me.

144
00:18:44,667 --> 00:18:51,614
Is this because I said you work hard,
but you'll never amount to anything?

145
00:18:52,716 --> 00:18:53,835
Mom.

146
00:18:53,835 --> 00:18:55,884
Honestly.

147
00:18:55,884 --> 00:18:59,043
But, Ha Yeon, it's true.

148
00:19:01,015 --> 00:19:04,440
- What did you say?
- So work harder.

149
00:19:04,440 --> 00:19:08,375
Find the drive to become something
and set a clear goal.

150
00:19:08,375 --> 00:19:10,816
Like your brother.

151
00:19:10,816 --> 00:19:14,396
Your brother had a clear goal, didn't he?

152
00:19:14,396 --> 00:19:16,834
He'd get into one of the top three, SKY,
no matter what.

153
00:19:16,834 --> 00:19:19,648
Then he'd get good grades
and join a big company.

154
00:19:19,648 --> 00:19:23,067
That's a clear, concrete goal.

155
00:19:23,665 --> 00:19:28,210
All I'm saying is, set a goal like that, too.

156
00:19:28,210 --> 00:19:31,018
Then I can support you, too.

157
00:19:31,018 --> 00:19:36,249
If you just drift along, day after day,

158
00:19:37,718 --> 00:19:42,348
with every day the same as the last,

159
00:19:42,348 --> 00:19:45,999
you'll never become anything.

160
00:19:45,999 --> 00:19:47,200
Understand?

161
00:19:49,688 --> 00:19:50,864
Ha Yeon.

162
00:19:50,864 --> 00:19:54,433
I'm only saying this because I care.

163
00:19:55,324 --> 00:19:57,375
It's all for your own good.

164
00:19:57,375 --> 00:20:02,042
But you take it the wrong way
and get all sulky.

165
00:20:02,042 --> 00:20:03,433
Yes, Mom.

166
00:20:05,292 --> 00:20:06,580
What?

167
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:09,244
Fine. I'll live my life your way, Mom.

168
00:20:09,244 --> 00:20:10,924
So you're going to set a goal?

169
00:20:10,924 --> 00:20:13,490
Yes, yes. I'll try setting a goal or something.

170
00:20:13,490 --> 00:20:16,882
Good. Good, Ha Yeon.

171
00:20:16,882 --> 00:20:23,556
Okay, so, first, make a daily
schedule and give it to me.

172
00:20:23,556 --> 00:20:27,773
Well, then, Mom, I'll be going for a walk
to clear my head.

173
00:20:27,773 --> 00:20:32,578
You said you'd set a goal,
so why are you suddenly going for a walk?

174
00:20:39,822 --> 00:20:41,724
Ha Yeon!

175
00:21:25,367 --> 00:21:27,003
Hey, did you see her?

176
00:21:32,584 --> 00:21:36,712
I heard she's from Seoul. Do you know her?

177
00:21:36,712 --> 00:21:38,589
No.

178
00:21:38,589 --> 00:21:42,384
But it looks like she fell for you
the second she got here.

179
00:21:42,384 --> 00:21:44,309
She knows what's good.

180
00:21:44,309 --> 00:21:46,250
Yeah, of course.

181
00:21:46,250 --> 00:21:48,604
Cho Yu Gyeom's looks are world-class.

182
00:21:48,604 --> 00:21:51,046
Hey, I'm at that level too. World-class?

183
00:21:51,046 --> 00:21:53,854
You're at that level. Economy class.

184
00:21:53,854 --> 00:21:56,400
He's at that level. World-class.

185
00:21:56,400 --> 00:21:58,374
Are you crazy, Lee Won Bae?

186
00:22:00,876 --> 00:22:02,207
Cho Yu Gyeom.

187
00:22:03,064 --> 00:22:05,843
You're meeting me at midnight tonight, right?

188
00:22:07,715 --> 00:22:13,998
But who knows? Maybe today is
the day you get to do what you want.

189
00:22:18,212 --> 00:22:20,257
Jin Mi, wait for me!

190
00:22:42,664 --> 00:22:44,554
You were here?

191
00:22:55,499 --> 00:22:59,295
But this is kind of scary.

192
00:22:59,295 --> 00:23:02,438
It's fine. I've got you.

193
00:23:02,438 --> 00:23:05,593
No, but I don't think I can do it.

194
00:23:05,593 --> 00:23:08,152
Then just close your eyes.

195
00:23:08,959 --> 00:23:11,889
Why can't we just go into the sea
from the beach?

196
00:23:12,474 --> 00:23:14,351
Didn't you say you can't swim?

197
00:23:14,351 --> 00:23:16,184
Yeah, I can't.

198
00:23:16,184 --> 00:23:20,338
Then you definitely can't.
The waves there are no joke at night.

199
00:23:22,192 --> 00:23:24,805
Then why is jumping down here okay?

200
00:23:24,805 --> 00:23:26,009
Big waves here, too.

201
00:23:26,009 --> 00:23:30,798
There are no waves down there.
It's totally safe as long as you jump.

202
00:24:41,230 --> 00:24:42,324
Hey...

203
00:24:44,328 --> 00:24:46,068
Let go of this so you can float.

204
00:24:46,068 --> 00:24:49,515
No... I'm just too scared.

205
00:24:50,781 --> 00:24:52,015
Just try letting go.

206
00:24:52,015 --> 00:24:53,876
- I'll help you.
- How?

207
00:24:53,876 --> 00:24:55,730
Wait a second.

208
00:25:03,419 --> 00:25:07,636
It's because we're lighter than the water.

209
00:25:09,768 --> 00:25:11,409
Look at the sky.

210
00:25:14,847 --> 00:25:17,885
It's always like this around here.

211
00:25:20,468 --> 00:25:22,321
Seoul isn't like this.

212
00:25:34,199 --> 00:25:36,119
Kim Ha Yeon.

213
00:25:36,119 --> 00:25:37,137
Yeah?

214
00:25:40,918 --> 00:25:42,187
Never mind.

215
00:25:44,501 --> 00:25:45,921
What is it?

216
00:25:47,838 --> 00:25:49,400
Nothing.

217
00:25:51,292 --> 00:25:53,218
I wanted to say thanks for coming.

218
00:25:53,218 --> 00:25:55,958
Seriously.

219
00:25:59,016 --> 00:26:01,518
- What?
- Don't let go, don't let go. I'm sorry,

220
00:26:01,518 --> 00:26:04,522
I'm sorry. Don't let go. I'm so sorry.

221
00:26:26,084 --> 00:26:27,238
It's me.

222
00:26:28,334 --> 00:26:30,834
Have you seen Cho Yu Gyeom today?

223
00:26:30,834 --> 00:26:32,600
No. Not since school ended.

224
00:26:33,397 --> 00:26:36,688
Where's Cho Yu Gyeom now? Is he home?

225
00:26:36,688 --> 00:26:39,961
Not sure. I haven't seen him since school.

226
00:26:39,961 --> 00:26:42,935
Has he been in touch? Did you go to his house?

227
00:26:42,935 --> 00:26:46,355
No? I asked to meet tonight,
but he said he had something to do.

228
00:26:46,355 --> 00:26:47,876
Didn't he?

229
00:26:47,876 --> 00:26:48,918
Yeah. Why?

230
00:26:50,691 --> 00:26:52,017
What was it?

231
00:26:52,017 --> 00:26:53,799
Wasn't he meeting you?

232
00:26:55,128 --> 00:26:56,532
Why? What's going on?

233
00:26:56,532 --> 00:26:58,168
Sung Sae Ryeong didn't see Cho Yu Gyeom?

234
00:26:58,168 --> 00:26:59,741
Seems so.

235
00:26:59,741 --> 00:27:04,850
Maybe his grandpa caught him
trying to sneak out.

236
00:27:04,850 --> 00:27:07,672
Or he fell off his bike and croaked.

237
00:27:14,208 --> 00:27:15,269
Look.

238
00:27:16,398 --> 00:27:17,943
Is this Cho Yu Gyeom's?

239
00:27:17,943 --> 00:27:19,375
Yeah.

240
00:27:19,375 --> 00:27:21,515
Shin Seung Chan!

241
00:27:21,515 --> 00:27:24,750
Hold on. Go check by the sea.

242
00:27:24,750 --> 00:27:27,847
What a pain, seriously.

243
00:27:30,042 --> 00:27:32,113
Are you here? Cho Yu Gyeom? You here?

244
00:27:33,264 --> 00:27:34,944
No, he's not here.

245
00:27:36,164 --> 00:27:37,928
He's not really dead, is he?

246
00:27:37,928 --> 00:27:39,920
Idiot. Hey.

247
00:27:39,920 --> 00:27:43,248
He might fall and die, but drown?
That guy's like a seal.

248
00:27:43,248 --> 00:27:47,868
What happened? What was it?

249
00:27:47,868 --> 00:27:51,748
Well, I'm at the cliff,
and only Cho Yu Gyeom's shoes are here.

250
00:27:51,748 --> 00:27:52,768
What?

251
00:27:53,437 --> 00:27:56,383
- What is it? What?
- What's wrong?

252
00:27:56,383 --> 00:27:57,593
What's this?

253
00:27:57,593 --> 00:28:00,428
What do you think? Sneakers.

254
00:28:00,428 --> 00:28:03,050
Don't you see? These aren't Cho Yu Gyeom's.

255
00:28:05,517 --> 00:28:07,397
You're right.

256
00:28:07,397 --> 00:28:08,404
I see.

257
00:28:10,468 --> 00:28:13,408
There's another pair of shoes
next to Cho Yu Gyeom's here.

258
00:28:13,408 --> 00:28:14,705
What?

259
00:28:15,527 --> 00:28:17,030
Whose are they?

260
00:28:17,030 --> 00:28:18,543
I don't know either.

261
00:28:18,543 --> 00:28:21,557
- Whose could they be?
- I'm asking whose they are!

262
00:28:21,557 --> 00:28:25,008
How should I know just from the sneakers?

