Then I'll tell you a very interesting story.

522
00:49:02,526 --> 00:49:03,751
Listen carefully.

523
00:49:06,277 --> 00:49:11,304
Because I'm going to kill you today.

524
00:49:12,722 --> 00:49:13,973
What did you say?

525
00:49:15,452 --> 00:49:20,082
My house is that three-story house
at the foot of the mountain over there, okay?

526
00:49:22,751 --> 00:49:25,337
Actually, that's not my house.

527
00:49:25,337 --> 00:49:29,090
What was it again?
A villa some lawmaker uses, I think?

528
00:49:29,090 --> 00:49:31,902
There's an old man there
who looks after the place.

529
00:49:32,587 --> 00:49:35,764
I got kind of close to him.

530
00:49:35,764 --> 00:49:39,487
So I go in and out of there
and clean it for him.

531
00:49:39,487 --> 00:49:41,020
What do you mean?

532
00:49:41,020 --> 00:49:42,868
What do I mean?

533
00:49:42,868 --> 00:49:47,300
The house everyone thinks is mine isn't mine.

534
00:49:48,194 --> 00:49:53,612
And my real house

535
00:49:53,612 --> 00:49:55,701
is farther in from there.

536
00:49:55,701 --> 00:49:58,671
It's a fucking tumbledown shack.

537
00:49:59,497 --> 00:50:03,070
I live there. With who?

538
00:50:03,070 --> 00:50:06,086
With my grandma, who can't hear or speak.

539
00:50:06,086 --> 00:50:10,280
How about that? I'm pitiful, aren't I?

540
00:50:14,553 --> 00:50:16,680
But the kids don't know.

541
00:50:16,680 --> 00:50:20,552
They just think my dad's
a lawmaker somewhere else.

542
00:50:21,977 --> 00:50:26,941
They think my mom went off to support Dad
and left me here alone,

543
00:50:26,941 --> 00:50:31,487
but actually, my dad's... in a gambling den.

544
00:50:31,487 --> 00:50:35,122
What does anyone do in a gambling den? Gamble.

545
00:50:35,866 --> 00:50:40,835
And my real mom ran away.

546
00:50:41,747 --> 00:50:47,377
She remarried some other guy
and abandoned me long ago.

547
00:50:51,799 --> 00:50:56,512
That's why I need Cho Yu Gyeom.

548
00:50:56,512 --> 00:51:01,016
Because Cho Yu Gyeom is my jackpot.

549
00:51:01,016 --> 00:51:03,978
- A jackpot?
- Yeah. A jackpot.

550
00:51:03,978 --> 00:51:08,941
Because he'll never take a single step
out of this town his whole life.

551
00:51:08,941 --> 00:51:13,466
Oh! Then I'm the perfect match.

552
00:51:13,466 --> 00:51:17,782
Of course he knows nothing about me.
But it doesn't matter.

553
00:51:17,782 --> 00:51:22,461
Because all I have to do
is marry into his family and have a son.

554
00:51:24,123 --> 00:51:25,925
What about Cho Yu Gyeom?

555
00:51:25,925 --> 00:51:30,150
He can't break up because he's scared of me?
That's even better.

556
00:51:30,150 --> 00:51:33,424
Then we'll just never break up.

557
00:51:33,424 --> 00:51:35,534
Then I'm happy I got my jackpot,

558
00:51:35,534 --> 00:51:38,438
and he's happy to have the prettiest
girl in our town.

559
00:51:38,438 --> 00:51:43,667
You see, we'll save each other that way.

560
00:51:43,667 --> 00:51:45,728
In a future without you.

561
00:51:51,442 --> 00:51:52,696
No.

562
00:51:54,236 --> 00:51:57,984
He might save you,
but I don't think you can save him.

563
00:51:57,984 --> 00:51:59,025
What?

564
00:51:59,025 --> 00:52:03,829
That's because he's a jackpot to you,
but you're a losing ticket to him.

565
00:52:03,829 --> 00:52:07,767
What are you saying, you psycho?
And here I was, letting you live.

566
00:52:08,529 --> 00:52:10,412
And Cho Yu Gyeom,

567
00:52:12,296 --> 00:52:13,953
I'll save him.

568
00:52:13,953 --> 00:52:16,128
He'll save me, too.

569
00:52:17,092 --> 00:52:18,792
Shut up!

570
00:52:36,820 --> 00:52:39,980
How dare you just show up out of nowhere!

571
00:53:54,440 --> 00:53:57,112
I never wanted to die.

572
00:54:01,482 --> 00:54:03,163
119, what's your emergency?

573
00:54:04,700 --> 00:54:06,042
Hello?

574
00:54:06,042 --> 00:54:11,373
- Excuse me... someone's dead here.
- Yes.

575
00:54:11,373 --> 00:54:13,000
What? Where are you?

576
00:54:13,000 --> 00:54:17,279
There's some kind of warehouse here.
It's a path along the rice paddies.

577
00:54:17,279 --> 00:54:19,131
I can see a road far off, too.

578
00:54:19,131 --> 00:54:23,889
Hello. Is the patient conscious and breathing?
Is the breathing normal?

579
00:54:25,679 --> 00:54:27,611
- There's blood...
- Hello?

580
00:54:27,611 --> 00:54:29,683
coming from the head... so much...

581
00:54:29,683 --> 00:54:31,689
Hello? Can you hear me?

582
00:54:32,478 --> 00:54:33,884
Hello?

583
00:54:35,342 --> 00:54:40,486
I just liked movies and believed in fate,

584
00:54:40,486 --> 00:54:45,518
and waited for my rich birth mother
and a prince on a white horse.

585
00:54:46,417 --> 00:54:49,083
I wanted to be just a notch above my brother,

586
00:54:49,083 --> 00:54:54,601
to say a single "no" to the friends
who bully me,

587
00:54:55,700 --> 00:54:58,574
to try having a boyfriend like everyone else,

588
00:54:58,574 --> 00:55:04,567
and to get into a car accident,
but only get a little hurt.

589
00:55:09,223 --> 00:55:11,618
And so summer came,

590
00:55:18,830 --> 00:55:21,149
and I came here,

591
00:55:22,634 --> 00:55:24,720
and that's really all I am.

592
00:55:28,334 --> 00:55:33,807
I never wanted to kill anyone.

593
00:55:36,333 --> 00:55:40,689
In this brilliant summer vacation.
